{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider was at the registered pickup point 'Blk 41 Sims Dr (shelter pickup)' for the whole waiting window and was never absent. His own device track carries 42 fixes, every one of them inside the 100 m rider-presence radius for a STANDARD zone, spanning 17:34:40 to 17:40:49, with a maximum distance of 11.74 m and a mean of 6.49 m from the pin, and a single recorded speed of 0.0 km/h. This is a rider who stood exactly where he was told to wait, in the rain, from before the driver tapped 'arrived' until the driver cancelled.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00621", "EV-TRIP-00621"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "At 17:35:40 the rider sent the only locating message in the log: 'please drive to the shelter, it's pouring'. The shelter is precisely the sub-location this trip records for pickup - 'Blk 41 Sims Dr (shelter pickup)' - so the rider named the correct pickup point, and identified which face of the location he was on, five minutes before the driver cancelled. That is the locating and coordinating conduct POL-NS-04(a) is written for, and it is also the statement that fixes the sub-location for the purpose of attributing any mislocation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00621", "EV-TRIP-00621"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver never closed the last stretch to the point the rider had named. His own telemetry puts his closest approach to the pin at 33.72 m across the entire trace and his mean distance at 296.72 m, while the rider sat 6.49 m from that same pin - the two devices never came near each other, and 'I was practically at the pin' is a statement the driver's own device contradicts. He answered 'you walk' at 17:36:20 and again at 17:37:10, and cancelled at 17:40:50 without moving. Whether or not the geofence reading puts him technically inside the 50 m radius, the policy's only fault-allocation rule for a failed pickup, POL-NS-03, looks to the chat log and puts the loss on the driver where the rider has stated the correct entrance or sub-location and the driver does not move to it. On this record the driver bears that loss and should take no compensation out of the rider's fee under POL-NS-07.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00621", "EV-CHAT-00621", "EV-TRIP-00621"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot stretch his hold with any advisory allowance. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00621-01, is MISSING - weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, 'no advisory covers the pickup road in this window' - and POL-NS-06(i) requires an advisory that is present and populated, so that limb is unavailable to him. There is in any event a single in-geofence interval on this trace (run_count 1, longest_run_sec 350.0), so there is no second interval to accumulate and the driver's hold must stand or fall on the one run the trace reports.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00621-01", "EV-GPS-00621"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available"
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not get POL-NS-04's automatic exoneration and does not pretend otherwise: limb (b) requires that the driver did not reply in the chat within 120 seconds of the rider's message, and the log shows the driver replied at 17:36:20, only 40 seconds after the rider's 17:35:40 message, with a second reply at 17:37:10. Limb (b) therefore fails on the clause's own terms and the clause does not apply to this trip. The rider's case rests on the arrival facts and on the fault allocation in POL-NS-03, not on POL-NS-04.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00621"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you were at the pickup. The rider's phone shows 42 fixes, a mean of 6.49 m and a maximum of 11.74 m from the pin at Blk 41 Sims Dr (shelter pickup), so she was genuinely waiting. The driver's trace shows him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from 17:34:50 and stationary there for a continuous 350 seconds. The fee is decided on the driver's side of that test, and it stands.\n\nPOL-NS-01 — all four limbs hold. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 17:34:52. (b) The GPS trace places him inside the 50 m pickup radius at 17:34:50, two seconds before that event. (c) The trace shows one continuous in-geofence run of 350 seconds, 17:34:50 to 17:40:40, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, measured from the first qualifying fix and not from the tap. (d) The trip record shows no boarding and a driver cancellation at 17:40:50 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, 30 seconds after the dwell elapsed.\n\nThe rider's points, answered. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance): I reject the argument that the driver should bear the loss. POL-NS-03 applies only where the driver is stationary OUTSIDE the 50 m arrival radius but within 400 m. His dwell was inside the radius — his closest approach to the pin was 33.72 m — so the clause's own precondition fails, and with it both the fault allocation and any pin-ambiguity goodwill (trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1 in any case). That the rider correctly named the shelter in chat at 17:35:40 therefore changes nothing. POL-NS-04: the rider does not get automatic exoneration, because the driver replied at 17:36:20, 40 seconds after the rider's 17:35:40 message and inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) fails on the clause's own terms. POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker): not engaged — the marker sits inside the geofence, not more than 300 m from the pin, and the recomputed dwell meets the minimum regardless. POL-NS-06 (short dwell): no shortfall — 350 seconds against a 300-second minimum is a surplus of 50 seconds. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00621-01 (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is immaterial: it can carry no fact, and with a single unbroken in-geofence run there are no separate intervals to sum.\n\nPOL-NS-08: the charged fee reconciles. The greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00, exactly the fare_breakdown cancellation-fee line and the SGD 4.00 charged, so there is no integrity defect.\n\nPOL-NS-07 and the outcome. With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, which is SGD 3.20, the residual SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 / 120 completed trips is 0.008 (below 0.08), so both limbs are unmet and compensation is payable. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is present. The driver's brief mentions the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter, which is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used; the trailing-window rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the counterparty-dispute counters are both 0. Under POL-GEN-03 this is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling: amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.20 figure as driver_compensation_sgd, and the rider's SGD 4.00 charge stands as recorded (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The rider's claim is not supported on this record and the disputed fee is not refunded.\n\nConfidence 0.90: every artifact that carries a deciding fact — the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — is at full weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Every artifact this brief rests on is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so no POL-GEN-02 disclosure discount applies to the driver's case. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00621-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0: under POL-GEN-02 its absence is itself citable but it can carry no fact. The driver expressly does NOT assert POL-NS-06 limb (i) — with a single unbroken 350-second in-geofence run there are no separate intervals to accumulate, so the missing advisory is immaterial to this ruling and the driver gains nothing and needs nothing from it.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00621-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This dispute is about the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged when the driver cancelled trip TRP-00621 at 17:40:50 on 21 Sep 2026 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nThe fee is chargeable. Under POL-NS-01 all four conditions hold. (a) EV-TRIP-00621 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 17:34:52. (b) EV-GPS-00621 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 17:34:50 — two seconds before that event — with 36 qualifying in-radius fixes and a closest approach of 33.72 m, so the POL-NS-02 arrival test is met on admissible fixes. (c) The trace shows one continuous in-geofence run of 350 seconds (17:34:50 to 17:40:40) against the 300-second STANDARD minimum: a surplus of 50 seconds, so there is no POL-NS-06 waiting-period shortfall. (d) EV-TRIP-00621 records no boarding event and a driver termination at 17:40:50 with RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell elapsed at 17:39:50.\n\nNo clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. POL-NS-04 does not apply: the rider did send a coordinating message at 17:35:40 and was genuinely at the pin (her own track shows 42 fixes, a maximum of 11.74 m and a mean of 6.49 m from the pin), but the driver replied at 17:36:20, 40 seconds later — inside the 120-second window — so limb (b) fails on the clause's own terms, as the rider accepts. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the 'arrived' marker sits inside the geofence, and even on a recomputed basis the corrected dwell still meets the minimum. POL-NS-03 does not apply either: it fires only where the driver held position for the dwell OUTSIDE the POL-NS-02 arrival radius while remaining within 400 m, whereas this driver held position inside the 50 m radius. The rider's argument that the driver 'never closed the last stretch' (closest approach 33.72 m) and the driver's own 'I was practically at the pin' are noted, but nothing in POL-NS-01 conditions the fee on crossing the final metres to a preferred sub-location, and POL-NS-03's own gate is not met. The rider's point that he named the shelter sub-location therefore does not move the fault allocation away from POL-NS-01.\n\nDriver compensation. POL-NS-07 applies: 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee is SGD 3.20, the residual 20 percent being retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 120 is 0.008 (below 0.08) — so compensation is payable and, per POL-NS-07 as read with POL-GEN-03, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd. The charged fee reconciles with the fee schedule: the STANDARD zone-class fee is SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee is SGD 4.00, the greater being SGD 4.00, exactly the fare_breakdown cancellation_fee, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. No POL-NS-09 trigger is present (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two artifacts contradict on arrival, dwell or rider presence, the counterparty-dispute counts are both 0, the anti-farming check does not trip, and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact).\n\nThe missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00621-01 (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact; its absence makes POL-NS-06 limb (i) unavailable, but because there is a single unbroken in-geofence run and no shortfall, the advisory is immaterial to this outcome. No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.90.\n\nOutcome for each side. For the rider: the claim is not supported on this record and the charge stands as presently recorded. For the driver: compensation of SGD 3.20 is payable. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty.",
    "confidence_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Every artifact this brief rests on is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so no POL-GEN-02 disclosure discount applies to the driver's case. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00621-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0: under POL-GEN-02 its absence is itself citable but it can carry no fact. The driver expressly does NOT assert POL-NS-06 limb (i) — with a single unbroken 350-second in-geofence run there are no separate intervals to accumulate, so the missing advisory is immaterial to this ruling and the driver gains nothing and needs nothing from it.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00621-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
